## Metadata
Title: FUN'S Cross-Word Puzzle
Author: Elizabeth M. Rutzinger
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1914-05-10
Number: 21
Description: A 19-wide diamond with a diamond-shaped hole in the centre (r6 c10 widening to r10 c6-c14 and narrowing to r14 c10; shown as _), so the middle column holds two short words (53-54 TULLE above the hole, 55-56 ILIAD below).
Source: Milwaukee Sentinel, 1914-05-10, p. 89
Solution-Source: Milwaukee Sentinel, 1914-05-17, p. 89


## Printed
heading: FUN'S
heading: CROSS-WORD PUZZLE
number: No. 21
intro: Miss Elizabeth M. Rutzinger, who sent in the ingeniously constructed cross word puzzle published in last week's FUN, has contributed another. And here it is. See if you can solve it. Fill in the small squares with words corresponding to the clews and definitions given herewith.
instructions: The answer to this puzzle will be published in next week's FUN.
solution heading: SOLUTION TO FUN'S CROSS-WORD PUZZLE No. 21


